":[{"text":"காக்கும்","lemma":"கா","gloss":"protecting"}],"gloss":"protecting"},{"surface":"நீள்","parts":[{"text":"நீள்","lemma":"நீள்","gloss":"ancient"}],"gloss":"ancient"},{"surface":"குடி","parts":[{"text":"குடி","lemma":"குடி","gloss":"lineage"}],"gloss":"lineage"},{"surface":"சிறந்த","parts":[{"text":"சிறந்த","lemma":"சிற","gloss":"excellent/distinguished"}],"gloss":"excellent"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தென்புலம்","parts":[{"text":"தென்புலம்","lemma":"தென்புலம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காவலின்","parts":[{"text":"காவலின்","lemma":"காவலின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஒரிஇப்","parts":[{"text":"ஒரிஇப்","lemma":"ஒரிஇப்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிறர்","parts":[{"text":"பிறர்","lemma":"பிறர்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"வன்புலம்","parts":[{"text":"வன்புலம்","lemma":"வன்புலம்","gloss":"harsh land"}],"gloss":"harsh land"},{"surface":"காவலின்","parts":[{"text":"காவல்","lemma":"காவல்","gloss":"protection"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of protection"},{"surface":"மாறி","parts":[{"text":"மாறி","lemma":"மாறி","gloss":"instead"}],"gloss":"instead"},{"surface":"யான்","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I"},{"surface":"பிறக்கே","parts":[{"text":"பிறக்கே","lemma":"பிறக்கே","gloss":"may I be born"}],"gloss":"may I be born","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Like a lion angry, with unyielding heart, / unsubmissive army kings together having united, / 'with me they will fight' they say, them / difficult battle to scream having attacked, with chariots / their back I do not see if, excellent / large beautiful kohl-rimmed eyes her from may I separate! / Virtue's state to deviate, of love in the assembly, / ability without a person having established, justice having deviated, / weak sceptre I who did may I become! Abundant fame / Vaigai surrounded strength having region's / unfailing wealth Maiyal chief / Mavan and, enduring fortress Anthai and, worthy / Anthuvan Sathan and, Athan Azhisi and, / fierce anger Iyakkan and, including others and, / eye like of friendship with friends mingled / sweet joy delight laughter having lost, I not only, / humanity protecting ancient lineage excellent / southern land protection from having abandoned, others' / harsh land protection of instead, may I be born!","translation":"They say that kings with unsubmissive armies, united together, will fight against me with an unyielding heart like an angry lion. If I do not attack them in a fierce battle making them scream, and see their backs as they flee with their chariots, may I be separated from her who has excellent, large, beautiful, kohl-rimmed eyes! May I become one who rules with a weak sceptre, deviating from justice, by establishing an incompetent person in the assembly of love where virtue should not deviate! Not only will I lose the sweet joy, delight, and laughter shared with friends who are as dear as my own eyes—including Mavan, the chief of Maiyal with its unfailing wealth surrounded by the Vaigai of abundant fame, Anthai of the enduring fortress, worthy Anthuvan Sathan, Athan Azhisi, and fierce-tempered Iyakkan—but may I also be excluded from protecting the southern land of my ancient, excellent lineage that protects humanity, and instead be reborn to protect the harsh lands of others!","modern":"கோபமடைந்த சிங்கத்தைப் போன்ற அடங்காத நெஞ்சமும், பணியாத படைகளும் கொண்ட பகை வேந்தர்கள் ஒன்று கூடி என்னோடு போரிடப் போவதாகக் கூறுகிறார்கள். கடுமையான போரில் அவர்கள் அலறும்படித் தாக்கி, அவர்களின் தேர்களுடன் அவர்கள் முதுகு காட்டி ஓடுவதை நான் காணாவிட்டால், சிறந்த பெரிய அழகிய மை தீட்டிய கண்களை உடைய என் மனைவியிடமிருந்து நான் பிரிவேனாக! அறநெறி தவறாத, அன்புடைய அவையிலே தகுதியற்ற ஒருவனை அமர்த்தி, முறை தவறி கொடுங்கோல் செலுத்தியவன் ஆவேனாக! மிகுந்த புகழுடைய வையை ஆறு சூழ்ந்த, வளம் மிக்க மையல் நாட்டின் தலைவனான மாவன், நிலைபெற்ற மதிலையுடைய ஆந்தை, புகழ் மிக்க அந்துவஞ் சாத்தன், ஆதன் அழிசி, கடுமையான சினமுடைய இயக்கன் ஆகியோருடனும், என் கண் போன்ற பிற நண்பர்களுடனும் கூடி மகிழ்ந்திருந்த இனிய களிப்பையும் சிரிப்பையும் இழந்தவன் ஆவேனாக! அதுமட்டுமன்றி, மக்களைக் காக்கும் நீண்ட குடிப்பெருமை வாய்ந்த தென்னாட்டைக் காக்கும் உரிமையை இழந்து, பிறருடைய வன்புலத்தைக் காக்கும் எளியவனாக மறுபிறவியில் பிறப்பேனாக!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Kañci tiṇai and the theme is Vañciṉak Kāñci (the vow of a king before going to war). The speaker is the Pandyan king Ollaiyūr Tanta Pūtappāṇṭiyaṉ, who vows to defeat his enemies who have underestimated his youth and strength. He declares that if he does not make his enemies flee in battle, he should suffer three terrible consequences: separation from his beloved wife, being remembered as a tyrant who ruled unjustly, and losing the companionship of his dearest friends while being reborn as a protector of harsh, alien lands instead of his glorious southern kingdom. The poem beautifully lists his close friends, showing the value he placed on loyalty and friendship, and highlights the high moral standards expected of a Tamil king. Key words include 'அவர்ப்புறம் காணேன் ஆயின்' (if I do not see their backs in retreat) and 'முறை திரிந்து மெலிகோல் செய்தேன் ஆகுக' (may I become one who rules unjustly).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}